export anchor MuseumPlacardStyle:
    number: 88
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Museum placard
    idea: The dashboard hangs on a vast white gallery wall, each project a framed colour field filled to its progress with a small neat wall label beside it, and every fact given an object number.
    base: light
    palette:
        wall: #fbfbf9, the page
        mat: #f6f3ec, the mats inside frames
        ink: #141414, text, slim frames, this week stems and the primary button
        labelGrey: #5e5e5e, captions, object numbers and quiet nav
        hairline: #dcdbd6, room rules, never text
        walnut: #3d2b1f, wooden frames
        gilt: #b59a5b, gilt frames, never text
        terracotta: #b0563a, the Design canvas
        cobalt: #2f4f7a, the Engineering canvas
        sage: #6f7f5a, the Research canvas
        ochre: #c99a3a, the Marketing canvas
        green: #276a3a, On track
        umber: #8a5a00, At risk
        red: #a1251b, Behind and overdue
    type:
        Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Nimbus Sans, Arial, sans-serif in light
        weights. The greeting is 72px at 200 tracked minus 0.02em, framed
        numbers 56px at 200, label titles 16px at 600, body 13 to 17px at
        300 with 1.5 line height, and room headings 13px caps tracked
        0.08em. Object numbers use SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas, monospace at
        11px in grey.
    layout:
        A slim header line with the bold brand, plain grey nav links with
        the current one underlined, an underlined search, a black New
        project button, a bare bell and the user. A title wall follows with
        120px of air above, Gallery 1 as a caption, a huge light Good
        morning, Mara and the date, and on the right a wall text behind a
        thin rule with a red square saying 4 tasks are overdue. Room 1
        hangs the four numbers as small black frames with a white mat,
        each with a placard of object number, title and one line. Room 2
        hangs six projects in three columns with big gaps, frames mixing
        walnut, gilt and slim black in portrait, landscape and square
        shapes. Each canvas is a pale field with a team colour block rising
        from the bottom to the percentage under a thin black line. Under
        each work a label gives the object number BW.2026.01 to 06, the
        name, team and year in italic, tasks, percentage and due date as a
        sentence, and the status. Room 3 lists activity with times in mono
        and Room 4 hangs the chart as a framed print of thin stems with
        round heads. Below 1000px works go two across, one on a phone.
    spacing: An 8px unit in large steps. 120px between rooms, 96px between works and 64px page margins on wide screens.
    density: Very sparse. One fact per frame, one short label per work and emptiness on purpose.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders: Thick frames of 14px walnut or gilt, or 6px black, around a 28px mat. Elsewhere only 1px hairlines.
    shadows: A soft drop below each frame, 18px down with negative spread, as if lit from above.
    icons:
        Almost none. Tiny line marks with the status word, an open circle
        for On track, an outlined triangle for At risk, a cross for Behind
        and a solid square for overdue.
    focus: A 1px ink outline offset 6px with a 1px grey ring further out at 11px, like a museum rope.
    tone: Quiet curatorial captions, such as Room 2, Projects in progress and Visitors are advised to begin with these.
